---
// Sequence to Shader case study (hero gradients). Every hero on this page is a live shader module served from
// /work/sequence-to-shader/<hero>/ (module, still/arc data or SVD textures, and a poster fallback).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const description =
  'Sequence to Shader, a Claude skill I built, turns animated gradients into live, lightweight web backgrounds: five heroes go from 17.1 MB of video to 200 KB.';
const dir = '/work/sequence-to-shader';
---

<Base title="Sequence to Shader · Nicholas Rode" description={description} image="/og/sequence-to-shader.jpg">
  <header class="hg-hero" id="hero">
    <div class="wrap hg-hero__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study · A Claude skill</p>
      <h1>17 MB of motion, delivered in 200 KB</h1>
      <p>Sequence to Shader is a Claude skill I built that turns animated gradients into live, lightweight web backgrounds. Here it is on five heroes: they load instantly, stay crisp on every screen, and keep their look frame for frame.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="hg-hero__tag">This hero is live · move your pointer</span>
  </header>

  <article class="wrap hg">
    <section>
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p class="lede">Animated gradients are everywhere on the web, and almost all of them ship as video. Video is heavy.</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Each one was a 3–3.5 MB file for a 5–6 second loop. On a slow phone connection that's 15–20 seconds of loading before the hero even shows up, which is longer than most people will wait. And if we ever wanted to change a color, say for a campaign or a dark mode, it meant going back into After Effects, exporting again and re-uploading.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">File size</span><span class="stat__value">~40 KB</span><span class="stat__was">instead of about 3.5 MB as a video</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Load time on a slow phone</span><span class="stat__value">0.3 s</span><span class="stat__was">instead of 15–20 seconds</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Look</span><span class="stat__value">Same</span><span class="stat__was">as the original, under 2% different, checked frame by frame</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The solution: a skill, not a one-off</h2>
      <p class="lede">Instead of hand-rebuilding every animation, I built a Claude skill that does it.</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Hand it the rendered frames and it looks at each animation, picks the right way to rebuild it, turns it into a small live component, and checks the result against the original frame by frame. It works on any rendered gradient, from any tool, and it's open source.</p>
        <p><a class="source" href="https://github.com/swicknick/sequence-to-shader">View the source on GitHub →</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who it's for</h2>
      <p class="lede">One change, four groups who get something different out of it.</p>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="card"><h3>Visitors: it's just there</h3><p>The hero arrives with the page instead of buffering after it, on any connection. The live heroes are drawn at the screen's own resolution, so they're as sharp on a large monitor as on a phone, and they respond to the cursor, which makes the page feel alive rather than played back.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Brand and marketing: colors become tokens</h3><p>On the live heroes, palettes are settings, not footage. A campaign color, a dark theme or a regional variant is a config change that ships the same day. Because color is applied as the final step, exactly as it is in the original animation, a new palette looks the way the motion designer would have made it, not like a tint on top.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Designers: nothing lost in translation</h3><p>Motion design stays in After Effects. Every hero was compared with the original frame by frame until the two were effectively identical, so what gets approved in the design file is what ships, with no "close enough" web version.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Engineers: a component, not an asset</h3><p>Each hero is a dependency-free component with one config object. It pauses itself when it's off-screen, honors reduced-motion settings, falls back to a still image on older browsers, and the live ones expose hooks for new interactions, with no video pipeline to maintain.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The five heroes</h2>
      <p class="lede">Every tile below is running live, not playing a video.</p>
      <div class="gallery">
        <div class="tile">
          <div class="tile__stage" id="t-wave" style={`background-image:url('${dir}/wave-star/poster.webp')`}></div>
          <div class="tile__body"><h3>Wave Star</h3><div class="tile__meta"><span class="chip good">2.98 MB → 27.1 KB</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tile">
          <div class="tile__stage" id="t-pill" style={`background-image:url('${dir}/pill-flower/poster.webp')`}></div>
          <div class="tile__body"><h3>Pill Flower</h3><div class="tile__meta"><span class="chip good">3.49 MB → 22.1 KB</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tile">
          <div class="tile__stage" id="t-moon" style={`background-image:url('${dir}/moon/poster.webp')`}></div>
          <div class="tile__body"><h3>Moon</h3><div class="tile__meta"><span class="chip good">3.51 MB → 57.7 KB</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tile">
          <div class="tile__stage" id="t-sphere" style={`background-image:url('${dir}/sphere/poster.webp')`}></div>
          <div class="tile__body"><h3>Sphere</h3><div class="tile__meta"><span class="chip good">3.54 MB → 41.6 KB</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Key decisions</h2>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="card"><h3>Computed live, not played back</h3><p>The heroes with sharp, sweeping folds are recreated from a single 16 KB image and the motion rules behind it, calculated every frame. That's why they never show a loop point and can be retimed, recolored or made interactive after launch, which no video can do.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>The right technique per hero</h3><p>Soft, drifting gradients compress beautifully into a few blended layers. Sharp moving folds don't, so those are computed live instead. Choosing per hero kept every one under 60 KB without trading away fidelity.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Calmer than the original</h3><p>A hero sits behind headlines and calls to action. I slowed every animation, some to a fraction of the original speed, so the motion sets a mood without competing for attention. Slowing a video that much would mean many times more frames and file size; here it's a single setting.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Considerate by default</h3><p>The animation rests whenever it's off-screen or the tab is hidden and stands still for visitors who ask their device for reduced motion. The live heroes also fade as you scroll past. Less battery, less distraction, more inclusive.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The outcome</h2>
      <p class="lede">Same animations, a fraction of the weight.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Hero</th><th>As video</th><th>Rebuilt</th><th>Smaller by</th><th>Slow mobile: video</th><th>Slow mobile: rebuilt</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Wave Star</td><td>2.98 MB</td><td>27.1 KB</td><td>112×</td><td>15.6 s</td><td>0.14 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Liquid Star</td><td>3.53 MB</td><td>51.1 KB</td><td>71×</td><td>18.5 s</td><td>0.26 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Pill Flower</td><td>3.49 MB</td><td>22.1 KB</td><td>161×</td><td>18.3 s</td><td>0.11 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Moon</td><td>3.51 MB</td><td>57.7 KB</td><td>62×</td><td>18.4 s</td><td>0.30 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sphere</td><td>3.54 MB</td><td>41.6 KB</td><td>87×</td><td>18.5 s</td><td>0.21 s</td></tr>
          </tbody>
          <tfoot>
            <tr><td>All five</td><td>17.1 MB</td><td>200 KB</td><td>87×</td><td>89 s</td><td>1.0 s</td></tr>
          </tfoot>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Video sizes use After Effects' standard web export. Load times assume a slow mobile connection.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What I learned</h2>
      <p class="lede">Small files were never the hard part. Fidelity was. A lighter hero that looks slightly off doesn't get shipped; matching the original frame for frame is what turned an almost 90× saving into something a brand team will sign off on.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Where this goes</h2>
      <p class="lede">When a hero costs kilobytes instead of megabytes, motion stops being a special-occasion asset reserved for the homepage. And because it's a skill, any team can do this with their own animations.</p>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="card"><h3>Motion on every page</h3><p>Product pages, campaign landers and launch announcements can all carry a living hero, with no performance budget spent and no compromise on load time.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>A motion language, not one-offs</h3><p>Palettes, pacing and moods become part of the design system. Every new hero starts from proven building blocks and stays unmistakably on-brand.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Heroes that respond</h3><p>Because each frame is drawn live, a hero can react to the visitor: the way they scroll, where their cursor rests, the story the page is telling.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>One brand, many moments</h3><p>Seasonal campaigns, dark themes and regional variants become a change of settings, so the brand can move as fast as the business does.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<!-- Served as-is (not bundled): the modules live in /public and load their own assets from basePath. -->
<script type="module" is:inline>
  import { WaveStarBackground } from '/work/sequence-to-shader/wave-star/wave-star-background.js';
  import { LiquidStarBackground } from '/work/sequence-to-shader/liquid-star/liquid-star-background.js';
  import { PillFlowerBackground } from '/work/sequence-to-shader/pill-flower/pill-flower-background.js';
  import { MoonBackground } from '/work/sequence-to-shader/moon/moon-background.js';
  import { SphereBackground } from '/work/sequence-to-shader/sphere/sphere-background.js';

  const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
  const live = [
    new LiquidStarBackground($('hero'), { basePath: '/work/sequence-to-shader/liquid-star/' }),
    new WaveStarBackground($('t-wave'), { basePath: '/work/sequence-to-shader/wave-star/', scrollFade: { enabled: false } }),
    new PillFlowerBackground($('t-pill'), { basePath: '/work/sequence-to-shader/pill-flower/textures/' }),
    new MoonBackground($('t-moon'), { basePath: '/work/sequence-to-shader/moon/textures/' }),
    new SphereBackground($('t-sphere'), { basePath: '/work/sequence-to-shader/sphere/textures/' }),
  ];
  for (const bg of live) bg.init().catch((e) => console.warn(e));
</script>

<style>
  .hg-hero {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    min-height: min(92svh, 860px);
    margin-top: -88px; /* sit under the nav, like the home hero */
    padding-top: 120px; /* copy never slides under the nav on short screens */
    display: grid;
    align-items: end;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #0b1033 url('/work/sequence-to-shader/liquid-star/poster.webp') center / cover;
    color: #fff;
  }
  /* Faint fade at the very top so the nav stays legible over the bright parts of the gradient.
     Painted after the shader canvas, below the copy, and never intercepts the pointer. */
  .hg-hero::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto;
    height: 160px;
    background: linear-gradient(rgba(13, 13, 15, 0.55), transparent);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hg-hero__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    width: 100%;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hg-hero .eyebrow {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .hg-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 88px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    max-width: 14ch;
  }
  .hg-hero p {
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px);
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: 0;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  .hg-hero__tag {
    position: absolute;
    right: 24px;
    bottom: 24px;
    z-index: 1;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }

  .hg {
    --good: #3ccf98;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }
  .hg section {
    padding-top: 72px;
  }
  .hg h2 {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 38px);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .hg h3 {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 66ch;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .cols,
  .gallery {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  /* Stats: one panel, three columns split by hairlines; label, value, comparison. Text-box trimming
     removes the font's invisible space above/below so the big values sit optically centred. */
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-top: 32px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 28px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .stat + .stat {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .stat__label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-box: trim-both cap alphabetic;
  }
  .stat__value {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.4vw, 52px);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    text-box: trim-both cap alphabetic;
  }
  .stat__was {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .cols,
  .gallery {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
  .card,
  .tile,
  .table-wrap {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .card {
    padding: 22px;
  }
  .card p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .tile {
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .tile__stage {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #111 center / cover;
  }
  .tile__body {
    padding: 16px 18px 18px;
  }
  .tile__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .chip {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .chip.good {
    color: var(--good);
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    min-width: 600px;
  }
  th,
  td {
    padding: 13px 16px;
    text-align: right;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  th:first-child,
  td:first-child {
    text-align: left;
  }
  th {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  tfoot td {
    font-weight: 700;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .source {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .source:hover,
  .source:focus-visible {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    max-width: 80ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .stats,
    .cols,
    .gallery {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .stat + .stat {
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .hg-hero__inner {
      padding-bottom: 48px;
    }
    .hg-hero__tag {
      right: 16px;
      bottom: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
